## Host ports

This checkout is **slot {{ slot }}** in devkit's `ports.toml`. Every published port
is its conventional base plus the slot:

| Service | Host port |
| --- | --- |
{{#app_service}}
| app | {{ app_port }} |
{{/app_service}}
{{#postgres}}
| postgres | {{ db_port }} |
{{/postgres}}
{{#redis}}
| redis | {{ redis_port }} |
{{/redis}}
{{#frontend}}
| vite | {{ frontend_port }} |
{{/frontend}}

Regenerate the `.env` block for any checkout with
`python <devkit>/scripts/devkit_ports.py <checkout-name>`.
{{/docker}}

{{#worktree}}
## Parallel worktrees

A second checkout runs its own stack side by side:

```bash
git worktree add ../{{ worktree }} {{ worktree }}
cd ../{{ worktree }}
cp ../{{ name }}/.env .env    # then replace the ports block — slot {{ worktree_slot }}
python <devkit>/scripts/devkit_ports.py {{ worktree }}
{{#docker}}
docker compose up -d
{{/docker}}
```

`COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` must equal the directory name in each. See `CLAUDE.md`,
"Parallel worktrees", for the rules that keep the two stacks independent.
{{/worktree}}

